==Old Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|gmq-osw|non|hverr}} (from {{der|gmq-osw|gem-pro|*hwarjaz}}) and {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{der|gmq-osw|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), which were conflated in (late) Old Norse. Most of the inflected forms of *''hwaz'' have since become obsolete, and what remains in form is essentially the descendant of *''hwarjaz'', but with an extra form for the neuter nominative and accusative singular: ''hvat'' from Old Norse {{m|non|hvat}}.

